.Dd October 17, 2026
.Dt PATINA-COMPOSITOR 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm patina-compositor
.Nd the Patina desktop's Wayland compositor
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -session
.Op Ar command ...
.Nm
.Fl h | V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a floating Wayland compositor: it owns the screen, the keyboard and
the pointer, places and draws windows, and starts the rest of the desktop
as its clients.
.Pp
It runs one of two ways, chosen by whether
.Ev WAYLAND_DISPLAY
is set when it starts:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Nested
As a window on another desktop (GNOME, sway, dwl), drawn with OpenGL ES,
or in software where there is none.
It quits when that desktop goes.
Its D-Bus names can't be served where another
.Nm
already serves them, so nested on a Patina session it wants a session bus
of its own:
.Dl dbus-run-session -- patina-compositor
.It On the hardware
From a text console or the login screen: it takes the GPU and the input
devices through the login session, and shows one monitor, the laptop's
panel first.
.El
.Pp
At start-up it runs Xwayland, when installed, for X11 apps;
.Xr patina-wallpaper 1 ,
.Xr patina-bar 1
and
.Xr patina-tiler 1 ;
then each
.Ar command
given.
Its keys run the launcher, the desktop's menu, the lock screen and the
volume flash, as configured below.
Every program it starts is listed with its output on Settings' Processes
page
.Pq Xr patina-settings 1 .
The wallpaper, the bar and the tiler are started again when they exit,
unless they exit five times within thirty seconds.
.Pp
Windows float: each is placed once, cascading beside the bar, and a click
focuses and raises it.
How windows tile is
.Xr patina-tiler 1 Ns 's
to decide: the compositor reports drags and Super with an arrow over the
session bus, and places windows where it's told.
Dragging a tiled window away restores it.
Where tiled windows meet side by side, the gap between them (or, without
gaps, the few pixels either side of where they touch) shows a left-right
arrow: dragging it grows the windows on one side as it shrinks those on the
other, keeping the gap, and the tiler keeps the new split.
Only the app's own maximise button (or a double click on its title bar)
maximises a window, edge to edge even with gaps.
The bar's tabs are the list of windows: Alt+Tab steps along them, and
closing a window gives the keyboard back to the window it came from, or,
if that's gone, focuses its neighbouring tab.
A window asking for fullscreen covers the whole screen, over the bar.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -session
Run as a login session: export
.Ev WAYLAND_DISPLAY ,
.Ev DISPLAY
and
.Ev XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP
to systemd and D-Bus, so services started later, such as
xdg-desktop-portal, reach this desktop.
On the hardware this is done anyway.
.Xr patina-session 1
passes it on from the login screen's entry.
.It Fl h , -help
Print a short usage message.
.It Fl V , -version
Print the version.
.El
.Sh KEYS
The defaults.
.Ic [keys]
in the config changes all but quitting, restarting, the consoles and the
media keys, within a second of a save.
.Bl -tag -width "Ctrl+Alt+Shift+Backspace"
.It Super , Super+Space
Open the launcher: Super tapped on its own, or with Space, as Cmd+Space
on a Mac.
.It Super+1 No to Sy 9
Bring forward the window in that tab of the bar.
.It Alt+Tab , Alt+Shift+Tab
Step to the next or previous tab.
.It Super+Q
Quit the focused app: ask all its windows to close.
.It Super+Up , Super+Down
Fill the screen with the focused window, tiled, and restore it; also
Ctrl+Super+K and Ctrl+Super+J.
.It Super+Left , Super+Right
Fill the left or right half of the screen; also Ctrl+Super+H and
Ctrl+Super+L.
These four are
.Xr patina-tiler 1 Ns 's
to decide, and do as it says.
.It Super+Shift+ Ns Ar arrow
Grow the focused window that way by a tenth of the screen.
.It Ctrl+Super+Shift+K , Ctrl+Super+Shift+J
Grow and shrink the focused window around its centre.
.It Ctrl+Super+Shift+L , Ctrl+Super+Shift+H
Widen and narrow it.
.It Super+Escape , Ctrl+Super+Q
Lock the screen.
.It Super+Shift+3 , Print
Save a screenshot of the desktop in
.Pa ~/Pictures/Screenshots .
.It Super+Shift+4
Save a screenshot of the focused window.
.It Ctrl+Space
Switch to the next keyboard layout, as on a Mac.
.It Super+Shift+R
Read the config file again.
.It Super+ Ns Ar key
Any other key with Super, or Super+Shift, goes to the focused window
with Ctrl in place of Super, as Cmd does on a Mac: Super+T opens a tab,
Super+W closes one, Super+C and Super+V copy and paste.
A terminal, whose desktop entry lists
.Cm TerminalEmulator
in its Categories, gets Ctrl+Shift instead, and Ctrl+Alt+Shift for
Super+Shift, so Super+D and Super+Shift+D stay apart there too.
Not while the screen is locked or a fullscreen window has the keyboard.
.It Ctrl+Alt+F1 No to Sy F12
Switch to that console, on the hardware.
.It Ctrl+Alt+Backspace
Quit, ending the session: the way out whatever state it's in.
.It Ctrl+Alt+Shift+Backspace
Restart the desktop without logging out, under
.Xr patina-session 1 .
Every window closes.
Refused while the screen is locked.
.El
.Pp
The brightness and volume keys change them, and
.Xr patina-volume 1
flashes up to show the level.
Super and a drag moves any window.
A right click on the empty desktop opens
.Xr patina-menu 1 .
On a touchpad, three fingers drag.
While the screen is locked, only the console and media keys work.
While a fullscreen window has the keyboard, as a game does, its keys go to
it: only Alt+Tab, Ctrl+Alt+Backspace, Ctrl+Alt+Shift+Backspace, the
console and the media keys still work, and tapping Super doesn't open the
launcher.
.Sh CONFIGURATION
The settings are in
.Pa ~/.config/patina-compositor/config.toml ,
written on first start with every setting commented out at its default.
Every key is optional.
Saving the file applies it within a second; mistakes are reported in the
log and never stop the desktop.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic scale
The screen's scale, such as 1.5.
Unset, it's chosen from the panel's density, or the parent desktop's when
nested.
.It Ic launcher
What tapping Super, or Super+Space, runs;
.Dq patina-launcher
by default, and
.Dq
for nothing.
.It Ic desktop_menu
What a right click on the desktop runs, given
.Fl -at Ar x , Ns Ar y ;
.Dq patina-menu
by default.
.It Ic [keyboard]
.Ic layout , variant , model
and
.Ic options
as in XKB, from
.Pa /etc/default/keyboard
when unset, the layouts as a list Ctrl+Space steps through,
.Dq us,se ,
four at most: XKB leaves out any after the fourth, which the log names;
.Ic repeat_delay
(milliseconds) and
.Ic repeat_rate
(per second);
.Ic caps_lock :
.Dq caps_lock ,
.Dq escape ,
.Dq ctrl
or
.Dq swap_escape .
.It Ic [touchpad]
.Ic tap
to click,
.Ic natural_scroll ,
.Ic speed
from -1.0 to 1.0, and
.Ic three_finger_drag .
.It Ic [cursor]
.Ic theme ,
an installed cursor theme instead of Patina's own, and
.Ic size
in pixels at scale 1.
.It Ic [media]
.Ic brightness_step
in percent;
.Ic volume_up , volume_down , mute
and
.Ic mic_mute ,
commands run through
.Xr sh 1
.Pq Xr wpctl 1 No by default ;
and
.Ic volume_menu ,
what flashes up after a volume key.
.It Ic [lock]
.Ic command ,
the lock screen
.Pq Dq patina-lock ,
any ext-session-lock locker;
.Ic on_suspend ,
whether to lock before the machine sleeps; and
.Ic on_screen_off ,
whether to lock when the screen turns off, as it does by default, on the
hardware.
.It Ic [screen]
.Ic off_after :
seconds without input before the screen turns off; 300 by default, 0
for never.
Any input turns it back on.
Something playing holds it on: a window using the idle-inhibit protocol,
or a holder of
.Sy org.freedesktop.ScreenSaver Ns 's
Inhibit, as Steam is while a game runs.
On the hardware the monitor is powered off; nested, it's only logged.
.It Ic [night_light]
.Ic mode :
.Dq off ,
.Dq always
or
.Dq schedule ;
.Ic from
and
.Ic to
as
.Dq HH:MM ;
and
.Ic temperature
in kelvin, from 6500 (neutral) to 1700.
On the hardware only.
.It Ic [gaps]
With
.Ic enabled
true, tiled windows (halves, and windows filling the screen) keep
.Ic size
logical pixels (8 by default, up to 64) around and between them, and
.Xr patina-bar 1
floats that far off the screen's edges with corners rounded by
.Ic radius .
Maximised windows still fill the screen edge to edge, and tiled ones keep
their rounded corners.
Off by default.
.It Ic [bindings]
Keys that run commands, such as
.Dl \(dqAlt+T\(dq = \(dqfoot\(dq
Modifiers (Super, Alt, Ctrl, Shift) and a key by its name.
.It Ic [keys]
The desktop's own keys, by action: one key or a list each, written as for
.Ic [bindings] ,
with
.Dq Super
alone for Super tapped on its own, as
.Dl snap_right = [\(dqSuper+Right\(dq, \(dqCtrl+Super+L\(dq]
An action set here replaces its defaults, and the rest keep theirs;
.Dq
or [] takes its keys away, and a Super key no action has goes to the app as
Ctrl.
The actions are
.Ic launcher , next_layout , next_tab , previous_tab , quit_app , lock ,
.Ic reload , screenshot , screenshot_window ,
.Ic snap_ Ns Ar side
and
.Ic grow_ Ns Ar side
(up, down, left, right),
.Ic resize_grow , resize_shrink , resize_wider , resize_narrower
and
.Ic window_1
to
.Ic window_9 ;
the config written on first start lists each with its keys.
An unknown action or key, or a key given two actions, is logged and left
out.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev WAYLAND_DISPLAY
Set: run nested in that desktop.
Unset: run on the hardware.
.It Ev PATINA_SCALE
The scale, over the config's.
.It Ev PATINA_RENDERER
.Dq pixman
draws in software, nested.
.It Ev PATINA_SESSION
Set by
.Xr patina-session 1 ,
which will start the compositor again: restarting is allowed, and a
screen locked before a crash starts locked.
.El
.Pp
Its clients get
.Ev WAYLAND_DISPLAY ,
.Ev DISPLAY
for Xwayland,
.Ev XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP Ns =Patina ,
a
.Ev PATH
with the compositor's own folder first, and
.Ev TERMINAL Ns =teleprinter
where it's installed, unless
.Ev TERMINAL
is set already: the terminal apps open.
.Sh SESSION BUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It com.sectorflabs.Patina.Processes
What the compositor started: List, Restart, Stop, Log, Spawn, and
RestartDesktop with the Supervised property.
For
.Xr patina-settings 1 ,
and for
.Xr patina-bar 1
and
.Xr patina-menu 1 ,
which start what they open through Spawn.
.It com.sectorflabs.Patina.Session
Lock, which runs the
.Ic [lock] command ,
and LogOut, which quits cleanly; for
.Xr patina-power 1 .
.It com.sectorflabs.Patina.NightLight
Night Light's state, overrides and inhibitors, on the hardware; see
.Xr patina-night-light 1 .
.It com.sectorflabs.Patina.Keyboard
The keymap's layouts (Layouts: each one's XKB layout, variant and name)
and the one in use (Current), announced as they change, and SetCurrent;
for the layout in
.Xr patina-bar 1 Ns 's
tray and
.Xr patina-settings 1 .
.It org.freedesktop.ScreenSaver
Inhibit and UnInhibit, which hold the screen on until let go of or until
the caller leaves the bus; SimulateUserActivity, as if there were input;
and GetActive, whether the screen is off.
Not served where another desktop already has the name.
.It com.sectorflabs.Patina.Tiling
Drags, Super with an arrow, the work area, and Resized for each tiled
window after the line between tiled windows is dragged, as signals; Windows,
WorkArea, Gap, Screen, Place, Restore, ShowPreview and HidePreview.
With gaps on, WorkArea is already inside the outer gaps, and Gap is the
gap to leave between windows.
The owner of
.Sy com.sectorflabs.Patina.Tiler
decides how dragged windows tile and what Super with an arrow does:
.Xr patina-tiler 1 ,
or a program that takes the name from it until it leaves the bus.
The compositor only reports them and places windows where it's told; with
no tiler, windows don't tile.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.config/patina-compositor/config.toml
The settings above.
.It Pa ~/Pictures/Screenshots/
Screenshots.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when it quits, 75 when it quits to be started again by
.Xr patina-session 1 ,
and 1 on an error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Try it as a window on the current desktop, with a terminal:
.Pp
.Dl $ patina-compositor foot
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr patina-bar 1 ,
.Xr patina-session 1 ,
.Xr patina-settings 1 ,
.Xr patina-tiler 1 ,
.Xr patina-desktop 7
